{"description":"Follow the work of TBA artist Nirbhai (nep) Singh Sidhu across three distinct architectural, historical, and cultural sites throughout Toronto.\nThis dedicated bus tour experience connects Sidhu’s work featured in the TBA Parallel Project Journey of the Mind at Campbell House Museum with the site of his permanent installation A Deathless Potential in Remembrance by You commissioned by the Toronto Biennial of Art, and his exhibition This song is dedicated to natures’ God at Capsules Artist Resources.\nMoving between a historic downtown museum and vibrant community spaces, this journey explores how art can create a space to reconnect with universal truths about the mind, revealing what connects us across different histories, cultures, and lived experiences and external labels.\nMembers of the without SHAPE without FORM team will be present throughout the tour to help ensure a comfortable experience and to share deeper insights into the ideas and practices that inform works.\nThe experience Includes\nGuided bus journey connecting all three sites.\nA complimentary Journey of the Mind zine to support continued creative reflection.\nA curated audio experience exploring the historical and cultural significance of each project, including moments of Simran (a practice of stillness and deep listening) and reflection.\nTime for self-guided exploration at each exhibition site.\nPresented by without SHAPE without FORM.\nFREE and OPEN TO ALL","organizer":"without SHAPE without FORM"}